-- ugcportal-qnq9.3: record, per upload, whether alcohol is visible, named or
-- clearly evoked.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-migrations prisma/migrations
-- --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script`; the comments are the only
-- hand-edit.
--
-- WHY THE COLUMN EXISTS. Norway's alkoholloven § 9-2 bans alcohol from
-- appearing in advertising for other products, and Helsedirektoratet's
-- examples include pictures that give a clear association with alcohol
-- *whatever the glass actually contains* (docs/ugc-research.md §3.1a). The
-- site's chosen angle is wine ACCESSORIES — empty glasses, coolers, tool-type
-- apps — which are monetisable precisely because they are not the drink. That
-- line is only enforceable if the record can tell the two apart, and until
-- this column there was nowhere to say which one an item is.
--
-- NULLABLE, WITH NO DEFAULT, AND THAT IS THE POINT — the same argument as
-- 20261006120000_add_minors_triage_fact. Every MediaListing row that already
-- exists gets NULL, which the gate reads as "not triaged" and refuses
-- (src/lib/resale-rights.ts, blocker `triage_incomplete`). A `DEFAULT 0`
-- would assert, about every upload anyone has ever listed, that no alcohol is
-- shown in it — an assertion no human has made, on a question where being
-- wrong is an administratively finable breach rather than a tidiness problem.
--
-- NO BACKFILL IS POSSIBLE HERE EITHER. "Is alcohol visible in this picture"
-- is answerable only by looking at the picture, and no SQL this migration
-- could write would be looking at anything.
--
-- RightsLayer gains ALCOHOL in the same change and needs no DDL: Prisma maps
-- enums to TEXT on SQLite, so the value is accepted by the existing
-- MediaRightsClearance.layer column the moment the schema declares it. Note
-- that a clearance row naming ALCOHOL settles nothing — the gate registers
-- the fact as `settledBy: "nothing"` and never looks for one — so this
-- migration creates no path by which an existing row becomes sellable.

-- AlterTable
ALTER TABLE "MediaListing" ADD COLUMN "depictsAlcohol" BOOLEAN;
